  "title": "Pakistani Man Sentenced to 27 Years for Plot to Kill Trump, US Officials",
  "summary": "Asif Merchant, a 48-year-old Iranian intelligence agent, was sentenced to 27 years in prison for plotting to assassinate Donald Trump in retaliation for the US killing of Revolutionary Guards commander Qassem Suleimani. The charges include the alleged hiring of a hitman to assassinate a U.S. official.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Asif Merchant, 48, was convicted of aiding the terrorist group that took credit for a suicide bombing at the Kabul airport five years ago during the US military’s withdrawal, and was sentenced to 20 years in prison.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The charges against Asif Merchant include the alleged involvement in a $126 million postage fraud case, which was reported by the Department of Justice.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Asif Merchant was found by court to have sought retribution over Qassem Suleimani's death.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
